drive straight down from their shrubby tops into deep water below.  The stone
is slick with a deep purple algae, almost black, which shows up between the
thriving patches of mussels and barnacles.  Deep cracks run vertically through
the stone, giving off a hissing sound as water rushes in and out.  Small green
crabs peek out, their mouths bubbling gently.  To the north is a thick kelp
bed, while to the east and west you can swim along the stone wall.
"
