"Although the water immediately around you is relatively calm, dangerous
currents to the east and south betray themselves by creating whorls in the
flotsam.  The cliffs to the north end gradually with several breaks,
terminating in a pinnacle of craggy stone.  Just between the stone spire and
the rest of the cliffs is a gap through which it might be possible to swim
without risking being swept into the depths.  The water gets gradually
shallower to the west, where a sand bar snuggles up against the cliffs.
